    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed two failing tests in the `frai-core` test suite:\n\n### 1. **Governance test failure** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`)\n**Problem**: The test tried to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export but it was only available in the default export.\n\n**Fix**: Added named exports in `src/finetune/index.js` for:\n- `APPROVAL_STATUSES`\n- `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`\n- `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`\n- `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n### 2. **Evaluation test failure** (`src/eval/index.test.js`)\n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function signature was `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be interpreted as banned terms, incorrectly flagging all outputs.\n\n**Fix**: Updated `toxicityMetric` signature in `src/eval/metrics.js` from:\n```javascript\nexport function toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)\n```\nto:\n```javascript\nexport function toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)\n```\n\nBoth changes maintain backward compatibility\u2014all public exports remain available. All 28 tests now pass.",
